{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"final","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Swimmer","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"Description","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Description"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This environment corresponds to the Swimmer environment described in Rémi Coulom’s PhD thesis"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tel.archives-ouvertes.fr\/tel-00003985\/document","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The environment aims to increase the number of independent state and control"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"variables as compared to the classic control environments. The swimmers"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"consist of three or more segments (’"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"links"}],"type":"strong"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":"’) and one less articulation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"joints (’"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"rotors"}],"type":"strong"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":"’) - one rotor joint connecting exactly two links to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"form a linear chain. The swimmer is suspended in a two dimensional pool and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"always starts in the same position (subject to some deviation drawn from an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"uniform distribution), and the goal is to move as fast as possible towards"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the right by applying torque on the rotors and using the fluids friction."}]},{"anchor":"Notes","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Notes"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The problem parameters are:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Problem parameters:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":": number of body parts","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"m","type":"text"},{"text":"i","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":": mass of part ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"i"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"i"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" ∈ {1…n})","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"l","type":"text"},{"text":"i","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": length of part "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"i"}]},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"i","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" ∈ {1…n})"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"k","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":": viscous-friction coefficient"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"While the default environment has "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" = 3, "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"l","type":"text"},{"text":"i","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" = 0.1,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"k"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" = 0.1. It is possible to pass a custom MuJoCo XML file during construction to increase the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"number of links, or to tweak any of the parameters."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"anchor":"Action-Space","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Action Space"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The action space is a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Box(-1, 1, (2,), float32)"},{"type":"text","text":". An action represents the torques applied between "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"links","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Num","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Action","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Control Min"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Control Max"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Name (in corresponding XML file)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Joint","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Unit","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"0"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Torque applied on the first rotor"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"-1"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"1"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"motor1_rot","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"hinge"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"torque (N m)"}]}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"1","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Torque applied on the second rotor","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"-1"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"1"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"motor2_rot","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"hinge"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"torque (N m)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]]},{"anchor":"Observation-Space","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Observation Space"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"By default, observations consists of:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"θ"},{"type":"text","text":"i"},{"type":"text","text":": angle of part "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"i","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" with respect to the "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"x","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" axis"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"θ","type":"text"},{"text":"i","type":"text"},{"text":"’: its derivative with respect to time (angular velocity)","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"In the default case, observations do not include the x- and y-coordinates of the front tip. These may","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"be included by passing ","type":"text"},{"code":"exclude_current_positions_from_observation=False","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" during construction.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Then, the observation space will have 10 dimensions where the first two dimensions","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"represent the x- and y-coordinates of the front tip.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Regardless of whether ","type":"text"},{"code":"exclude_current_positions_from_observation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" was set to true or false, the x- and y-coordinates","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"will be returned in ","type":"text"},{"code":"info","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with keys ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"x_position\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"y_position\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", respectively.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"By default, the observation is a ","type":"text"},{"code":"ndarray","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with shape ","type":"text"},{"code":"(8,)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" where the elements correspond to the following:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"| Num | Observation                          | Min  | Max | Name (in corresponding XML file) | Joint | Unit                     |","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"| — | ———————————— | –– | — | –––––––––––––––– | —– | ———————— |","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"| 0   | angle of the front tip               | -Inf | Inf | free_body_rot                    | hinge | angle (rad)              |","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"| 1   | angle of the first rotor             | -Inf | Inf | motor1_rot                       | hinge | angle (rad)              |","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"| 2   | angle of the second rotor            | -Inf | Inf | motor2_rot                       | hinge | angle (rad)              |","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"| 3   | velocity of the tip along the x-axis | -Inf | Inf | slider1                          | slide | velocity (m\/s)           |","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"| 4   | velocity of the tip along the y-axis | -Inf | Inf | slider2                          | slide | velocity (m\/s)           |","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"| 5   | angular velocity of front tip        | -Inf | Inf | free_body_rot                    | hinge | angular velocity (rad\/s) |","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"| 6   | angular velocity of first rotor      | -Inf | Inf | motor1_rot                       | hinge | angular velocity (rad\/s) |","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"| 7   | angular velocity of second rotor     | -Inf | Inf | motor2_rot                             | hinge | angular velocity (rad\/s) |","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"anchor":"Rewards","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Rewards"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The reward consists of two parts:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"forward_reward"}]},{"type":"text","text":": A reward of moving forward which is measured"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forward_reward_weight"},{"text":" * (x-coordinate before action - x-coordinate after action)\/dt","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"dt","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the time between actions and is dependent on the frame_skip parameter"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(default is 4), where the frametime is 0.01 - making the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"dt = 4 * 0.01 = 0.04","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":". This reward would be positive if the swimmer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"swims right as desired."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"ctrl_cost"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":": A cost for penalising the swimmer if it takes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"actions that are too large. It is measured as ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ctrl_cost_weight"},{"text":" *","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sum(action","type":"text"},{"text":"2","type":"text"},{"text":")","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" where ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ctrl_cost_weight"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" is a parameter set for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"control and has a default value of 1e-4","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The total reward returned is ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"reward"}],"type":"strong"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"="}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"forward_reward - ctrl_cost"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"info"},{"text":" will also contain the individual reward terms","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"anchor":"Starting-State","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Starting State"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All observations start in state (0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0) with a Uniform noise in the range of [-"},{"code":"reset_noise_scale","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"reset_noise_scale","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"] is added to the initial state for stochasticity."}]},{"anchor":"Episode-End","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Episode End"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The episode truncates when the episode length is greater than 1000."}]},{"anchor":"Arguments","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Arguments"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No additional arguments are currently supported in v2 and lower."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["gym.make('Swimmer-v4')"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"v3 and v4 take gym.make kwargs such as xml_file, ctrl_cost_weight, reset_noise_scale etc.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["env = gym.make('Swimmer-v4', ctrl_cost_weight=0.1, ....)"]},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Parameter"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Type"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Default","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Description","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"xml_file","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"str","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"swimmer.xml\""}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Path to a MuJoCo model"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forward_reward_weight"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"float"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"1.0","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Weight for "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"forward_reward"}]},{"type":"text","text":" term (see section on reward)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"ctrl_cost_weight","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"float"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1e-4"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Weight for "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"ctrl_cost"}]},{"type":"text","text":" term (see section on reward)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"reset_noise_scale","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"float"}],"type":"strong"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0.1"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Scale of random perturbations of initial position and velocity (see section on Starting State)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"exclude_current_positions_from_observation"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"bool"}],"type":"strong"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"True"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether or not to omit the x- and y-coordinates from observations. Excluding the position can serve as an inductive bias to induce position-agnostic behavior in policies"}]}]]]},{"anchor":"Version-History","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Version History"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"v4: all mujoco environments now use the mujoco bindings in mujoco>=2.1.3","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"v3: support for gym.make kwargs such as xml_file, ctrl_cost_weight, reset_noise_scale etc. rgb rendering comes from tracking camera (so agent does not run away from screen)","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"v2: All continuous control environments now use mujoco_py >= 1.50","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"v1: max_time_steps raised to 1000 for robot based tasks. Added reward_threshold to environments."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"v0: Initial versions release (1.0.0)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/org.liuliu.s4nnc\/documentation\/Gym"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/org.liuliu.s4nnc\/documentation\/Gym\/Env","doc:\/\/org.liuliu.s4nnc\/documentation\/Gym\/MuJoCoEnv"],"title":"Conforms To"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/org.liuliu.s4nnc\/documentation\/Gym\/Swimmer"},"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/gym\/swimmer"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"class","roleHeading":"Class","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Swimmer"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Swimmer"}],"modules":[{"name":"Gym"}],"title":"Swimmer","externalID":"s:3Gym7SwimmerC"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/org.liuliu.s4nnc\/documentation\/Gym\/Swimmer\/init(forwardRewardWeight:ctrlCostWeight:resetNoiseScale:)"],"title":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/org.liuliu.s4nnc\/documentation\/Gym\/Swimmer\/data","doc:\/\/org.liuliu.s4nnc\/documentation\/Gym\/Swimmer\/model"],"title":"Instance Properties"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/org.liuliu.s4nnc\/documentation\/Gym\/Swimmer\/Env-Implementations"],"title":"Default Implementations"}],"references":{"doc://org.liuliu.s4nnc/documentation/Gym/Swimmer/model":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.liuliu.s4nnc\/documentation\/Gym\/Swimmer\/model","abstract":[],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/gym\/swimmer\/model","title":"model","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"model"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6MuJoCo7MjModelV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MjModel"}],"kind":"symbol"},"https://tel.archives-ouvertes.fr/tel-00003985/document":{"titleInlineContent":[{"text":"“Reinforcement Learning Using Neural Networks, with Applications to Motor Control”","type":"text"}],"type":"link","identifier":"https:\/\/tel.archives-ouvertes.fr\/tel-00003985\/document","title":"“Reinforcement Learning Using Neural Networks, with Applications to Motor Control”","url":"https:\/\/tel.archives-ouvertes.fr\/tel-00003985\/document"},"doc://org.liuliu.s4nnc/documentation/Gym/Swimmer/Env-Implementations":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Env Implementations","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.liuliu.s4nnc\/documentation\/Gym\/Swimmer\/Env-Implementations","url":"\/documentation\/gym\/swimmer\/env-implementations","abstract":[],"role":"collectionGroup"},"doc://org.liuliu.s4nnc/documentation/Gym":{"type":"t